Article 2 For the purposes of these Regulations, the following terms shall have the meanings ascribed to them:
(1) "Integrated circuit" means a semiconductor integrated circuit, that is, a product, in an intermediate or final form, which has two or more elements, at least one of which is an active element, and some or all of the interconnections integrated in or on a piece of semiconductor material to perform an electronic function;
(2) "Layout-design of an integrated circuit" (hereinafter referred to as layout-design) means the three-dimensional disposition of two or more elements, at least one of which is an active element, and some or all of the interconnections of an integrated circuit, or such a three-dimensional disposition prepared for the manufacture of an integrated circuit;
(3) "Holder of the right in layout-design" means the natural person, legal person or other organization that enjoys the exclusive rights in a layout-design in accordance with these Regulations;
(4) "Reproduction" means the act of reproducing a layout-design or an integrated circuit incorporating such a layout-design;
(5) "Commercial exploitation" means the act of importing, selling or otherwise providing a protected layout-design, an integrated circuit incorporating such a layout-design, or an article incorporating such an integrated circuit for commercial purposes.

Article 7 The holder of the right in a layout-design shall enjoy the following exclusive rights:
(1) To reproduce the protected layout-design as a whole or any original part thereof;
(2) To commercially exploit the protected layout-design, an integrated circuit incorporating such a layout-design, or an article incorporating such an integrated circuit.

Article 16 For an application for registration of a layout-design, the following shall be submitted:
(1) An application form for registration of the layout-design;
(2) A reproduction or a drawing of the layout-design;
(3) Where the layout-design has been commercially exploited, a sample of the integrated circuit incorporating such layout-design shall be submitted;
(4) Any other materials as prescribed by the intellectual property administrative department of the State Council.

Article 23 The following acts may be performed without the permission of, and without the payment of remuneration to, the holder of the layout-design right:
(1) Reproducing the protected layout-design for personal purposes or solely for the purposes of evaluation, analysis, research, or teaching;
(2) Creating an original layout-design on the basis of the evaluation or analysis of the protected layout-design carried out in accordance with the preceding subparagraph;
(3) Reproducing or commercially exploiting a layout-design that has been independently created by the actor and is identical to another layout-design.
